## CHAPTER FIVE: SUMMARY, CONCLUSION, AND RECOMMENDATIONS

### 5.1 Summary of Findings
The DOU Transit app successfully digitizes Keke operations, ensuring that the campus transport ecosystem is cashless, secure, and easily monitored by the administration.

### 5.2 Conclusion
By migrating to React Native and solidifying the Kotlin backend, the project achieves a scalable architecture capable of handling thousands of concurrent student requests during peak hours.

### 5.3 Recommendations
- Student Affairs should strictly enforce the physical QR code stickers on all campus Kekes.
- Future work should include offline Bluetooth Low Energy (BLE) payments for areas with poor internet connectivity on campus.

